  "issue_number": 3391,
  "issue_title": "Add absolute-timestamp tooltip to <TimeAgo> relative times",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`TimeAgo` (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/time-ago.tsx`) renders relative time (\"2m ago\") in a bare `<span>{text}</span>` with no `title` attribute, so there is no way to see the actual timestamp on hover \u2014 confirmed by reading the component (lines 21-25). This is the single most-used time component in the frontend (59 call sites across routes and components), so the gap is felt everywhere a relative time appears. The fix already has prior art: `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts` exports `formatFreshnessAbsolute(updatedAt)`, a null-safe `new Date(x).toLocaleString()` helper, and five separate components (`methodology-callout.tsx`, `schema-drift-detail.tsx`, `charts/stat-with-spark.tsx` \u00d72, `charts/spark-legend.tsx`, `states/registry-empty.tsx`) each hand-wire `title={freshAbs ?? undefined}` around their own relative-time text using it. `panel-shell.tsx:82` goes further and puts a raw ISO string directly in `title={meta?.generatedAt}` on a wrapper `<span>` around a nested `<TimeAgo>` \u2014 i.e. callers are already reaching for exactly this tooltip behavior by duplicating a wrapper around `TimeAgo`, rather than getting it from `TimeAgo` itself.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd an absolute-timestamp `title` tooltip directly to `<TimeAgo>` so every one of its 59 call sites gets hover-to-see-exact-time for free, using the existing `formatFreshnessAbsolute` helper instead of introducing a new formatter \u2014 this is a small, targeted enhancement to one shared component, not a new feature surface.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File to change: `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/time-ago.tsx` (the entire component is lines 1-26; the `<span>` to add `title` to is lines 21-25).\n- Import `formatFreshnessAbsolute` from `@/lib/metagraphed/freshness` (same helper `methodology-callout.tsx`, `schema-drift-detail.tsx`, `stat-with-spark.tsx`, `spark-legend.tsx`, and `states/registry-empty.tsx` already import) and compute the tooltip value from the component's existing `at` prop.\n- Critical edge case to handle correctly: `formatFreshnessAbsolute` only checks `Number.isNaN(t.getTime())`, so on its own it renders the 1970-01-01 registry placeholder as a real (misleading) date like `\"12/31/1969, 5:00:00 PM\"` instead of suppressing it. `TimeAgo`'s visible text already suppresses the placeholder correctly because `formatRelative` internally gates on `isUsableTimestamp` (`> 2000-01-01`). The tooltip must use the same gate \u2014 e.g. only pass `title` when `isUsableTimestamp(at)` is true (or equivalently, skip the title whenever the visible `text` is the `\"\u2014\"`/fallback case) \u2014 so a row that correctly shows \"\u2014\" never shows a bogus 1969 date on hover.\n- What \"done\" looks like: the rendered `<span>` gets a `title={...}` attribute holding the absolute local-time string (e.g. via `formatFreshnessAbsolute(at) ?? undefined`, gated as above) whenever `at` is a usable timestamp, and no `title` (or `undefined`) when `at` is missing, unparseable, or the 1970 placeholder \u2014 mirroring the existing fallback/mounted branching already in the component (`!at ? fallback : mounted ? formatRelative(at) : \"\"`).\n- No coordination needed with another issue: `formatFreshnessAbsolute` and its tests already exist and ship independently of this change; this issue only wires it into `TimeAgo`. Part of the Wave 3 tracker (#2542), \"Search + entity-page UX\" bucket.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/time-ago.tsx` is the only component file changed (plus its colocated test file, if one is added)\n- [ ] `<TimeAgo>`'s rendered `<span>` has a `title` attribute set to the absolute timestamp (via `formatFreshnessAbsolute` or equivalent) when `at` is a valid, usable timestamp\n- [ ] The `title` is absent/`undefined` when `at` is `null`/`undefined` (fallback case) \u2014 matches current no-tooltip behavior, just doesn't regress it\n- [ ] The `title` is absent/`undefined` when `at` is the `1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z` registry placeholder (or any other pre-2000 date) \u2014 does not leak a misleading absolute date on hover for a row whose visible text is \"\u2014\"\n- [ ] No existing `TimeAgo` caller needs to change (the 59 existing usages keep compiling/rendering unchanged; callers that today wrap `TimeAgo` in their own `title`-bearing element, e.g. `panel-shell.tsx`, are unaffected since JSX only applies the outermost `title`)\n- [ ] `npm run build` / typecheck passes with the new import wired in\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not change `formatRelative`, `isUsableTimestamp`, or any other export in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/format.ts` \u2014 the relative-text logic is out of scope, only the tooltip is being added.\n- Do not touch the five existing hand-rolled `title={freshAbs ?? undefined}` call sites (`methodology-callout.tsx`, `schema-drift-detail.tsx`, `stat-with-spark.tsx`, `spark-legend.tsx`, `states/registry-empty.tsx`) or `panel-shell.tsx`'s wrapper `title` \u2014 deduplicating those onto the new built-in `TimeAgo` tooltip is a separate follow-up, not part of this issue.\n- No backend/API involvement \u2014 this is a pure frontend/presentation change to one client component.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: XS \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
